     FOUR-STROKE ENGINE SIMULATOR
     Otto (Petrol) & Diesel Cycles — Animate · Learn · Practice · Quiz

     Thermodynamic model: air-standard cycle evaluated between BDC and
     TDC, with a residual-gas / charge-heating balance for state 1 and a
     separate real air-fuel ratio used for fuel flow, BSFC and brake
     thermal efficiency. The gap between the air-standard efficiency and
     the brake thermal efficiency is the point of the tool, so both are
     computed honestly and shown side by side.

     References: Cengel & Boles, Thermodynamics: An Engineering Approach,
     9th ed., Ch. 9 (Gas Power Cycles); Heywood, Internal Combustion
     Engine Fundamentals, 2nd ed., Ch. 5 and 6.
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

  /* ── 1. Constants ── */
  var GAMMA = 1.4;                 // ratio of specific heats, cold air standard
  var R_GAS = 0.287;               // kJ/(kg·K) — air
  var CV    = R_GAS / (GAMMA - 1); // 0.7175 kJ/(kg·K)
  var CP    = CV * GAMMA;          // 1.0045 kJ/(kg·K)
  var P_ATM = 101.325;             // kPa
  var LHV   = { petrol: 44000, diesel: 43000 };   // kJ/kg lower heating value
  var AFR_STOICH = { petrol: 14.7, diesel: 14.5 };

  /* ── 2. State ── */
  var st = {
    mode: 'simulate',
    fuel: 'petrol',
    /* geometry */
    bore: 86, strokeLen: 86, nCyl: 4, cr: 10.5, rodRatio: 3.5,
    /* operating point */
    rpm: 2500, pMan: 101.325, qin: 1350, afr: 14.7,
    etaMech: 0.86, pExh: 105, tIn: 300,
    /* valve timing, degrees */
    ivo: 12, ivc: 48, evo: 48, evc: 12,
    /* display */
    units: 'si', pane: 'pv', preset: 'sedan',
    showParticles: true, showEquation: true, showGrid: true,
    showLabels: true, showPumping: true,
    /* Slowest by default: at 1x a 2500 rpm engine turns 15 000 deg/s,
       which is 20 cycles a second and unwatchable. This is a viewing
       control only — the physics always uses the real rpm. */
    animSpeed: 0.05
  };

